// Yes this file is intentionally (almost) empty!
// ---
// Having a blank `tsconfig.json` file prevents TypeScript from crawling up your directory tree
// and possibly picking up a parent `tsconfig.json` (which, unsurprisingly, is very hard to debug).
//
// `"include": []` makes this config compile NOTHING. Without it, an empty `{}` defaults to
// `**/*`, so any tool that picks this config (e.g. an editor TS server resolving a stray file)
// would pull EVERY package below this directory into one program — which merges the per-frontend
// `i18n.d.ts` `declare global { interface NeckarI18nKeys ... }` augmentations and reports a bogus
// "cannot simultaneously extend" conflict. Each frontend is meant to be its own program.
{
  "include": []
}
